&lt;h4&gt;Personal Buying experience&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior UX Researcher&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior UX Researcher (IC3)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Lille&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timing: ASAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context &amp;amp; project&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decathlon’s mission is to bring people together through sport and make wellbeing accessible for all. To make this mission a reality, Decathlon relies on In-Store teammates who embody the human touchpoint between our brand and our customers, and are key enablers of Store business. This is exactly where your mission comes in: unlocking a deep understanding of our in-store teammates to identify key pain points and turn them into clear business opportunities. Working in a dynamic omnichannel context, you will partner closely with product teams to guide the creation of simple, efficient, and field-adapted experiences—enabling our teammates to be as impactful as possible with our customers while bridging the gap between user needs, business goals, and technological opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Digital plays a pivotal role in the quality of the connection built during moments shared between customers and teammates. How? By ensuring every In-Store Decathlonian works in an efficient and adapted environment that seamlessly supports their daily tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this context, we’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;UX Researcher&lt;/strong&gt; to dive into In-Store behaviors and elevate the &lt;strong&gt;Personal Buying Experience&lt;/strong&gt;. Your mission will be to uncover the needs and friction points of our teammates on the floor, identify and build strong opportunities, while supporting our product team in their craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;User Researcher&lt;/strong&gt;, you will enrich our &lt;strong&gt;User Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt; and drive the tangible impact of your findings on our in-store tools. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decode the field:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct in-store observations to map the real-world practices, workflows, and pain points of our store teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guide decision-making:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn qualitative and quantitative data into actionable strategic insights to shape the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Promote a User-first culture:&lt;/strong&gt; Feed our team&#39;s knowledge repository to align Designers, Product Managers, and Tech leads with the reality on the shop floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role &amp;amp; responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Designer / Researcher, you will act as a &lt;strong&gt;key partner with cross-functional product teams&lt;/strong&gt; to&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;influence and enlighten decisions&lt;/strong&gt;, whether long-term strategy, quarterly roadmaps or day-to-day tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;build a &lt;strong&gt;shared understanding / empathy&lt;/strong&gt; of the current customer experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensure that we identify and tackle &lt;strong&gt;the most relevant opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;build long-term impact&lt;/strong&gt; (outcomes) rather than features (outputs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;build and feed a long term &lt;strong&gt;user and customer knowledge strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Craft / Core skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Framing -&lt;/strong&gt; Support product decisions (product outcomes, opportunities, solutions) through research insights and Opportunity Solution Trees (OSTs) / Identify and prioritize research plans with stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research / Problem Discovery -&lt;/strong&gt; Uncover and refine opportunities through qualitative and/or quantitative research / Map end-to-end journeys &amp;amp; opportunity spaces / Make your findings easily accessible and understandable to your stakeholders (readouts, documentation, etc.) / Support teams to setup continuous discovery “habits” (eg. regular &amp;amp; holistic insights gathering, insights library, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Discovery &amp;amp; Testing -&lt;/strong&gt; Support designers &amp;amp; product trios by actively contributing to design critiques &amp;amp; test sessions / Provide research methodology guidance when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusivity &amp;amp; Ethics -&lt;/strong&gt; Craft research methodologies &amp;amp; outputs that fully include the diversity of our users and tackle possible biases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behaviors / Soft skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence -&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely and proactively with all expertises (product, business, engineering, countries, etc.) to influence strategies, prioritization and discovery/delivery roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional collaboration (functional management) -&lt;/strong&gt; Involve your product teams and stakeholders throughout your research/design process, leveraging the right methods and/or storytelling, creating a safe environment for feedbacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design collaboration - &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute to elevate the research practices, run and/or participate to collaborative design sessions with your peers across multiple teams (New Business Models, eCommerce, InStore, …)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth mindset -&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify and build on your strengths and improvement areas, turn failures into positive learning lessons (for you and for others)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behaviors / Soft skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence&lt;/strong&gt; - Work closely and proactively with all expertises (product, business, engineering, etc.) to influence strategies, prioritization and discovery/delivery roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional collaboration &lt;/strong&gt;- Involve your product team and stakeholders throughout your design process, leveraging the right methods and/or storytelling, creating a safe environment for feedbacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design collaboration&lt;/strong&gt; - Contribute to elevate the design practice, run and/or participate to collaborative design sessions (co-design, design critiques) with your peers across multiple teams (New Business Models, eCommerce, …)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth mindset&lt;/strong&gt; - Proactively identify and build on your strengths and improvement areas, turn failures into positive learning lessons (for you and for others)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join the In-Store adventure?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here are a few challenges you may tackle if you join the In-Store adventure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enhance the human bound&lt;/strong&gt; - Simplifying complexity and leveraging store teams and management, building more and more quality time spaces between our customer and our teammate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve Store efficiency&lt;/strong&gt; - Empower our teammates on the field, understand their pain-points and provide strong, efficient and scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reinforce the end-to-end, omni experience&lt;/strong&gt; - Contribute to an high &amp;amp; amazing end-to-end experience for our customer, by designing the best digital experience for our teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design the store of tomorrow&lt;/strong&gt; - Leverage on digital to support the store evolution, and design the futur of our actual main touchpoint with the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Store might be a perfect match for you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to support the teammates, and be at the heart of Decathlon&#39;s ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love collaborating with a wide variety of expertises &amp;amp; stakeholders (your product team, but also people from eCom, Business, Countries, Sports, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to be part of a lovely &amp;amp; united team, always ready to help each other or share good laughs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to play a key role in transforming Decathlon’s stores !&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible working:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 days of remote work per week;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work locations:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to work from any Decathlon Digital office in Lille, Paris, or Nantes;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-quality gear:&lt;/strong&gt; Equipment provided in line with your mission and our social commitments (Mac, Windows, or Chromebooks);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global reach:&lt;/strong&gt; A local project team within a worldwide network (offering international career opportunities);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skill development:&lt;/strong&gt; Continuous growth and support (diverse projects, technical certifications from year one, internal and external training, etc.);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation package:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive package (employee profit-sharing, monthly/quarterly bonuses).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL CONTEXT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What if technology allowed us to push the boundaries and take sports experiences to new levels? That&#39;s exactly our goal at Decathlon Digital! We are a team of 5,000+ experts in software engineering, product management, data, cloud, and cybersecurity, distributed across Paris, Lille, and Amsterdam. Together, we are creating the largest digital sports platform, leveraging tech innovation from design to value chain optimization, connected experiences and product second life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changing the game for good&lt;/strong&gt;. We are in this for the love of sports. And like everything we love, we want it to last. That’s why we are embarking on a journey to create a more sustainable tech model, reducing our direct environmental impact while maintaining a safe, diverse, and inclusive space for all our people to learn and thrive together. Team up with us to design the digital future of sports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AlphaSense:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is the AI platform redefining market intelligence and workflow orchestration, trusted by thousands of leading organizations to drive faster, more confident decisions in business and finance. The platform combines domain-specific AI with a vast content universe of over 500 million premium business documents — including equity research, earnings calls, expert interviews, filings, news, and internal proprietary content. Purpose-built for speed, accuracy, and enterprise-grade security, AlphaSense helps teams extract critical insights, uncover market-moving trends, and automate complex workflows with high-quality outputs. With AI solutions like Generative Search, Generative Grid, and Deep Research, AlphaSense delivers the clarity and depth professionals need to navigate complexity and obtain accurate, real-time information quickly. For more information, visit &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.alpha-sense.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.alpha-sense.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. Come join us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Content organization is responsible for identifying, creating or licensing and integrating best-in-class unstructured and structured content into the AlphaSense platform. The team reports to the Chief Content Officer and has strategy, product and content management, collection operations and support responsibilities for each Content vertical. We have been experiencing rapid growth across all content sets. We value and uphold transparency, trust, and accountability in our relationships within the Content teams and with external partners and internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Product Manager for New Content Evaluation and Analysis to help us expand and strengthen the breadth, quality, and value of the data and content that power our Platform. Candidates should have deep knowledge of capital markets and investment research combined with extensive experience of evaluating and integrating financial research content and AI-powered investment analysis workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Major Areas of Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify the Need and Showcase the Value:&amp;nbsp; Help identify and evaluate third-party quantitative and qualitative datasets and content for the needs of the AlphaSense platform (e.g. market data, fundamentals, estimates, ESG, news, research, transcripts, regulatory filings, and alternative data). Work alongside Partnership Management and Content Leads to assess data quality, methodology, licensing terms, and integration feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Due Diligence Effort: Run point individually or leading a due-diligence analyst team on active vendor evaluations, including data trials, support proofs of concept, and own the framework to evaluate coverage, timeliness, accuracy, and history analysis. Help build content org-wide business case for new datasets and quantify value proposition, cost, buy vs build impact, and strategic fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a Use Case Expert for AlphaSense content. Contribute to market research and competitive analysis to identify net new opportunities for innovation and differentiation. Identify new high impact AI-driven functionality and data sets and formulate the licensing target vendor or self-sourcing strategy to introduce new content into the AlphaSense platform and agentic workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market Research and Assessment: Track industry trends and competing platforms, solutions, and content to deliver competitive intelligence and better evolve product and content vision. Keep abreast of a rapidly evolving competitive landscape and client expectations along with unprecedented LLM and AI workflow advances.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have genuine excitement and passion for corporate finance, capital markets, and investment research coupled with data management expertise demonstrated either in previous capacity at a buy-side or sell-side firm or you have successfully supported AI products/features/data used by investment and data analysis professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have natural enthusiasm for working at the intersection of AI, data, technology, and investment research and track record of expert-level data analysis at scale using traditional data query or generative AI tools and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have the energy and enthusiasm to work in a high-paced, high-growth environment and you are comfortable accommodating rapidly changing business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent presentation skills with demonstrated ability to inform and influence executives and align with multiple levels of stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have driven successful due diligence project outcomes or run content evaluations with diverse businesses and teams across multiple locations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate empathic communication, with the ability to listen and identify problems in need of solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of work experience at a leading financial institution or investment research platform firm focused on the delivery or evaluation of content, features, analytics, and models for front-office investment professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient knowledge of contemporary market data and investment research databases, products, and workflow tools (e.g.: Fundamentals, Estimates, Transactions data, Ownership data, Market data, News, Transcripts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the logical structure of relational and JSON databases. Demonstrated experience of running complex data queries and analyses using traditional data- query or contemporary generative AI techniques is required. Close familiarity and hands-on experience with Claude Code or similar platforms is a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to collaborate with a dedicated cross-functional product development or evaluation teams of engineers, content leads, and vendor management professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of successful collaboration and delivery with a globally distributed team is a must. Prior formal or informal team leadership experience is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to set priorities, stay focused, and meet or beat deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc degree or material academic background in a quantitative analysis field&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in content acquisition and licensing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a market intelligence or financial research SaaS start-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to iterative / agile development methodologies in the context of product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with and leading distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is an equal-opportunity employer. We are committed to a work environment that supports, inspires, and respects all individuals. All employees share in the responsibility for fulfilling AlphaSense’s commitment to equal employment opportunity. AlphaSense does not discriminate against any employee or applicant on the basis of race, color, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, age, religion, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, military or veteran status, disability, or any other non-merit factor. This policy applies to every aspect of employment at AlphaSense, including recruitment, hiring, training, advancement, and termination.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;In addition, it is the policy of AlphaSense to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified employees who have protected disabilities to the extent required by applicable laws, regulations, and ordinances where a particular employee works.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
